                        ],
                        "form": "die Hexenringe"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2132fb7-9461-3faa-b986-e62f601d52ea",
                        "entry_id": "4475b5a1-6966-3395-aafa-3f540ba87b2b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "konzentrischer grüner Ring auf einer Viehweide, der sich durch üppigen Graswuchs auszeichnet, während das Land umher die nackte Erde zeigt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d329f232-9dcf-4582-a5b8-bae870796c51",
                                "sense_id": "b2132fb7-9461-3faa-b986-e62f601d52ea",
                                "text": "Hierbei sieht man an der Peripherie des Myzels ringförmige Zonen, die Hexenringe, in welchen der Graswuchs stimuliert wird und auch solche, in der das Gras unter dem Einfluß des Pilzmyzels abstirbt."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "08329146-d6ed-3056-9158-6bc0d79cf26f",
                        "entry_id": "4475b5a1-6966-3395-aafa-3f540ba87b2b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "kreisförmige Ansammlungen von Pilz-Fruchtkörpern, die dadurch entstehen, dass das Myzel eines Pilzes in alle Richtungen gleich schnell wächst"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Mykologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aef48a55-686c-4be7-89fa-1bcd553e0cb0",
                                "sense_id": "08329146-d6ed-3056-9158-6bc0d79cf26f",
                                "text": "Anhand der Ausbreitungsgeschwindigkeit des Pilzes und des Radius eines Hexenrings kann man auch das Alter des Pilzes bestimmen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4ef1cd02-ca9f-3414-9c2e-f2752da9127e",
                        "entry_id": "4475b5a1-6966-3395-aafa-3f540ba87b2b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "kreisförmig ausgetretene Grasnarben, die in der Brunftzeit der Rehe entstehen können, wenn der Rehbock die Ricke treibt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Jägersprache"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c49db5e9-b2d3-4768-ad8d-30a22ca839fd",
                                "sense_id": "4ef1cd02-ca9f-3414-9c2e-f2752da9127e",
                                "text": "„Bei einem Halt bewindet meist der Bock ausgiebig den Schürzenbereich der Ricke, worauf oft das Treiben, jetzt in immer enger werdenden Kreisen, fortgesetzt wird. Die Spuren dieses kreisförmigen Treibens in der Bodenvegetation sind die bekannten Hexenringe.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7f79b43c-775e-40fe-b54d-2d90e3221ae8",
                        "source_entry_id": "4475b5a1-6966-3395-aafa-3f540ba87b2b",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2132fb7-9461-3faa-b986-e62f601d52ea",
                        "target_lang_word": "rond de sorcière",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rond de sorcière",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94c688cc-f9ac-3339-9622-9c4078323a92",
                                        "entry_id": "9c944845-7fa5-3685-a8ae-e27405aea9fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vaste cercle, sur un terrain, au pourtour duquel croissent des champignons."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28976c8d-3bf0-4775-97ab-7ef0fb9859da",
                                                "sense_id": "94c688cc-f9ac-3339-9622-9c4078323a92",
                                                "text": "Le ramassage se poursuivit en direction d'une zone dégagée légèrement en creux. Schobert fut persuadé d'avoir découvert, formant un magnifique rond de sorcière, des psalliotes des prés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40fc46a8-7894-43f8-9327-3677d1449aaf",
                                                "sense_id": "94c688cc-f9ac-3339-9622-9c4078323a92",
                                                "text": "Les spécimens peuvent alors former un « rond de sorcière » qui mérite ici davantage le nom de « cercle de fée ». Malgré leur petite taille, les jeunes spécimens se repèrent très facilement sur le sol […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14dd6a31-709d-4cff-9da1-32d16c31da2d",
                        "source_entry_id": "4475b5a1-6966-3395-aafa-3f540ba87b2b",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2132fb7-9461-3faa-b986-e62f601d52ea",
                        "target_lang_word": "anillos de hadas",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "18335621-e720-44e7-97a7-01c854f07128",
                        "source_entry_id": "4475b5a1-6966-3395-aafa-3f540ba87b2b",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2132fb7-9461-3faa-b986-e62f601d52ea",
                        "target_lang_word": "corros de brujas",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a375fed7-c306-4ba2-995d-bcabff2fb651",
                        "source_entry_id": "4475b5a1-6966-3395-aafa-3f540ba87b2b",
                        "source_sense_id": "08329146-d6ed-3056-9158-6bc0d79cf26f",
                        "target_lang_word": "fairy ring",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fairy ring",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fc0ebb7-fbe9-3f08-9f8a-d3eaf7232f83",
                                        "entry_id": "4f04cbcc-1c7c-3040-9d4e-8c0fdbf43368",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place where fairies congregate in a ring, particularly in order to dance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5710e355-4fcd-4882-9854-8a1511851e02",
                                                "sense_id": "7fc0ebb7-fbe9-3f08-9f8a-d3eaf7232f83",
                                                "text": "They are fond of music and dancing. It is their dancing that forms the fairy rings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25e10d81-d26d-4081-b026-d2fc6cb4c7f2",
                                                "sense_id": "7fc0ebb7-fbe9-3f08-9f8a-d3eaf7232f83",
                                                "text": "1914, \"Rhys at the Fairy Dance\" in Maud Keary, Enchanted Tulips and Other Verses for Children, Macmillan and Company, page 102,\nThough many a year has passed away, / None have seen Rhys since that day! / Does he dance and does he sing / For ever in a Fairy Ring?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63a08e74-1860-4734-8342-493c22fa16cc",
                                                "sense_id": "7fc0ebb7-fbe9-3f08-9f8a-d3eaf7232f83",
                                                "text": "Welsh folklore also reveals few references to fairy rings but there is a fine example found in the legend \"Rhys at the Fairy Dance\" (collected in 1827) in which Rhys is lost but found again when several people venture to a nearby fairy ring."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a6da63f-b2ef-3f83-8b40-7f20428b9b0e",
                                        "entry_id": "4f04cbcc-1c7c-3040-9d4e-8c0fdbf43368",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ring of fungi marking the periphery of the perennial underground growth of the mycelium."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b453af5d-8854-4cbb-870e-0cd31815a06e",
                                                "sense_id": "8a6da63f-b2ef-3f83-8b40-7f20428b9b0e",
                                                "text": "This curious phenomenon has been differently accounted for. The following is Mr. Nicholson's description and explanation: \"the appearance in the grass, says he, commonly called Fairy Rings, is well known. It consists either of a ring of grass of more luxuriant vegetation than the rest, or a kind of circular path in which the vegetation is more defective than elsewhere. It appears to be pretty well ascertained that the latter state precedes the former. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f2497a6-175a-4c0b-8e13-c1fdd956a118",
                                                "sense_id": "8a6da63f-b2ef-3f83-8b40-7f20428b9b0e",
                                                "text": "The best known Fungus occupant of fairy rings is the Fairy Ring Agaric or Champignon, Marasmius oreades, termed in the older botanical textbooks Agaricus oreades."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e548d10-374e-4445-8a1e-92b5d284dbc0",
                                                "sense_id": "8a6da63f-b2ef-3f83-8b40-7f20428b9b0e",
                                                "text": "So writing it down and reading it later, I realized somehow my subconscious was giving me a warning of things to come. In the dream I woke up at the height of the full moon in my garden. I didn't realize that in my drunken stupor I had fallen asleep amidst a fairy ring. A fairy ring is a bunch of mushrooms growing in a circle. I often see them growing on lawns. Legend has it that if one gets caught in this circle on a full moon, the fairies will take him or her captive and do as they please."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
